From cb1df17c2b7fec0913b747e4648c300f7f4f928a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:15:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): hub CPU sampler keeps rolling 1 s
 snapshots so every reported triple fits the Board's 2 s window

The thread sampler (430a8d4464) took one ~1 s sample every 5 s and the report attached the newest one up to 10 s
old. The Board keeps a triple only when at - 2000 <= cpu_busy_sample_end_ms <= at (hermes-hub mailbox.ts
CPU_MAX_DELAY_MS, deployed d9e950ade108), so with independent sampler and reporter clocks only ~35-40 % of
CPU-bearing reports were stored, and each rejected one erased the stored sample.

AdvisorySampler now reads one /proc/stat snapshot per WINDOW_S on its own thread and forms each sample from
(previous, new) with machine_cpu_metrics.between (the window bounds and arithmetic cpu.sample now shares). An
out-of-bounds window drops that sample and restarts from the new snapshot; the next snapshot is scheduled from
the previous one's read time, so an early wake never shortens a window. The advisory file is still written at
most every 5 s, from the newest valid sample. take(limit) returns the newest unreported sample measured under the
same limit only when its end stamp is 0..1500 ms before the take (REPORT_MAX_AGE_MS replaces REPORT_MAX_AGE_S=10).

Tests: the real sampler thread and the real Reporter on a lockstep fake clock with 3-20 s sync rounds (every
triple <= 1500 ms old at send, >= 9/10 due reports carry one, never reported twice, advisory never stale), and
the Board rule with 0-400 ms send latency and sampler stalls (100 % accepted).

Card t_01a1cf00956ad8b2.
